    "snippet": "---\ntitle: Press, Media, Interviews Radio, Television, Book Reviews Opinion, Podcasts\ndate: 2012-08-10\n---\nPress, Media, Interviews\n\nRadio, Television, Book Reviews Opinion, Podcasts\n\nInterviews\n\nInterviews were conducted from 1995 to 2022 with worldwide radio and television entities:\n\nCNBC-Africa\n\nSABC, Johannesburg\n\nAl Jazeera, Qatar\n\nRadio 702, Johannesburg\n\nSABC-TV , Cape Town\n\nCarte Blanche, South Africa\n\nAustralian Broadcasting Corporation\n\nBBC World Service, London\n\nMonitor Radio, London\n\nBloomberg TV , London\n\nFrance Internationale, Paris\n\nThis Day Live (Abuja, Nigeria)\n\nYouTube: AfricaUnauthorised\n\nRadio and/or television interviews also took place in Canberra, Dakar, Nairobi, Kampala, Marrakech, Tunis, Lagos, Wellington, Maputo, Dar-es-Salaam, Antananarivo and Windhoek.\n\nPeter Day on BBC World Service discusses with Duncan Clarke Africa's Future: \n\nPress interviews took place also in Dar-es-Salaam, Maputo, Cape Town, Antananarivo, Rio de Janeiro, London, Singapore, Tokyo, Houston, Marrakech, Harare, Dakar, Calgary and Paris.\n\nOn 'How to be an Africa Expert', see Opinion in Business Day: \n\nInterview on Al Jazeera, March 2013 on Brics and South Africa \n\nDuncan Clarke on Africa's oil and gas future in GeoExpro, 2015: \n\nOpinion Pieces\n\nArticles, book reviews or opinion pieces or comments on works were published by press in Africa, Europe, United States, Canada and Japan - notably:\n\nPress & Media\n\nInternational Herald Tribune\n\nThe Economist\n\nBusiness Day (South Africa)\n\nAfrica.org.\n\nNational Geographic\n\nDow Jones\n\nReuters\n\nBloomberg\n\nJeune Afrique (Paris)\n\nThe Citizen (South Africa)\n\nBeeld (South Africa)\n\nFAO Global Magazine (Rome)\n\nThis Day (Nigeria)\n\nSunday Times (Johannesburg)\n\nAfrican Business (London)\n\nNikkei (Tokyo)\n\nDrum Magazine\n\nBusiness Times Magazine\n\nGuardian Africa Network\n\nHuffington Post\n\nIrish Times\n\nBrenthurst Briefing (Johannesburg)\n\nHarare News\n\nWorld Oil Industry\n\nPetroleum Africa, PetroMin Asia, Hydrocarbons Asia, Petroleum News Southeast Asia, Petrole Information, African Petroleum Journal"
