    "score": 0.7195554971694946,
    "snippet": "---\ntitle: Duncan Clarke\nauthor: Duncan Clarke Home About All Books More\ndate: 2025-01-01\n---\nCategoriesNew & TrendingDeals & RewardsBest Sellers & MoreMembershipsCommunitiesMoreMoreYour Books\n\nAn error has occurred, please refresh the page.\n\nAn error has occurred, please refresh the page.\n\nAn error has occurred, please refresh the page.\n\nAn error has occurred, please refresh the page.\n\nAn error has occurred, please refresh the page.\n\nAn error has occurred, please refresh the page.\n\nAn error has occurred, please refresh the page.\n\nAn error has occurred, please refresh the page.\n\nDuncan Clarke was born in Salisbury, Rhodesia, in 1948. After St George's College, 1960-65, and Rhodes University, 1966-69, he graduated Ph.D (Economics), University of St. Andrews, Scotland, 1975. He founded Global Pacific & Partners, 1978-2016. Since 1970 he has published numerous books on Rhodesia, Zimbabwe and Africa, and on world oil and gas, during a 'safari' across 127 countries on Six Continents. About more on 50 years of writing, see  New on Amazon: Accidental Author: Fifty Years Writing, Africa and the World, 2023 Forthcoming on Amazon: The Quiet Rhodesian: Silent Servant, 1909-1981 - in late 2023 Praise for Published Books: The Last Rhodesians: Society Adrift 'I'm in awe of this portrait of white Rhodesia. The mastery of detail is astonishing, the sheer intellectual power extraordinary.'. Michael Holman, Financial Times, ex-Africa editor and author of Postmark Africa. Rhodes' Ghost: The Conquest of Zambesia 'I don't know how many books have been written about Cecil John Rhodes, but 'Rhodes'' Ghost' might be close to the final word on this extraordinary man.'. Hannes Wessels, AfricaUnauthorised, and A Handful of Hard Men; The SAS and the Battle for Rhodesia. Africa's Future: Darkness to Destiny 'A richly detailed review of Africa''s past and about the future … Indispensable for anyone interested in global trends in the 21st century.' Ian Morris, Why the West Rules — For Now"
