    "snippet": "---\ntitle: Five Rock Bands Making A Comeback\nauthor: About the Creator this is a placeholder Jessica Farrington\ndate: 2025-01-01\n---\nFive Rock Bands Making A Comeback\n\nRock artists booming with new releases.\n\nMany rock artists from the late 90's - early 2000's are making their way back into the world with new songs, covers, and tours. For some reason, I have yet to uncover, many of the famous musicians from the early 2000's fell of the grid until the past two or three years when many of them have once again taken to the stage.\n\nHere are 5 Rock Bands who are making a comeback.\n\n1. Volbeat\n\nVolbeat is a rock band formed in 2001 from Copenhagen, Denmark. The band was signed by Dutch Label Mascot Records. They released four albums within the span of five years starting in 2005. Volbeat took a three-year break before releasing their fifth album, 'Outlaw gentlemen & and Shady Lady's' in 2013. They waited another three years before once again creating new masterpieces in 2016. Since then they have released two more albums.\n\n2. Evanescence\n\nEvanescence was formed in Little Rock, Arkansas by Lead singer and pianist Amy Lee and Guitarist Ben Moody. They released their first album, 'Fallen,' in 2003 with Wind-up Records. The band managed to earn two Grammy Awards after selling 17 million copies of the album. Through several changes in the band lineup they managed to produce two more albums by 2006 including their live album, 'Anywhere But Home.' The band took a five year break before coming back with their self-titled album in 2011. The band disappeared for another five years before releasing the album, 'Lost Whispers.' Evanescence took on a different kind of project and released an orchestrated album, 'Synthesis', with a new take on their best songs from their previous albums in 2017 and a live version in 2018. Though there has been no new music released of late Evanescence continues to tour worldwide and there is rumor of a possible new album soon.\n\n3. Halestorm\n\nHalestorm is a rock band formed by Lead Vocalist Lzzy Hale and her brother, Arejay Hale, who plays drums. Guitarist"
