    "snippet": "---\ntitle: Alleviate Release Their Debut Album, 'DMNS'\nauthor: Matt Benton\ndate: 2024-08-10\n---\nThe hottest new band of the year is gearing up to release their debut album, and it is sure to be a contender for one of the best releases of the year. Hailing from Germany and comprised of members from several different bands to form an almost metalcore/post-hardcore supergroup, Alleviate is here to take the music scene by storm. Effortlessly combining elements from different genres such as djent, deathcore, metalcore, and post-hardcore, Alleviate has a sound that sets them apart from the rest. Within 5 years of forming, the band has already amassed over 70,000 monthly listeners on Spotify with over two million plays across their releases, and the band is on the track of success. Alleviate is gearing up to release their debut album, DMNS, on the 23rd of August via Arising Empire. I was lucky enough to get a sneak peak at the album, and all I can say is: Holy Shit.\n\nThe album from start to finish sounds like a giant breakdown full of some of the best playing and singing I think I've ever heard before. Between the beautiful balance of the dual vocals of Timo's singing and Marius's screams, each song sounds like a duet from a play or metal opera. Nothing seems forced and everything just sounds so polished! The guitar playing from Ramon & Marc is just as beautiful as the dual vocals. From heavy as fuck breakdowns and riffs to tantalizing chord work, I keep finding myself with my jaw on the ground. A band is nothing without a powerhouse drummer and that is absolutely evident with Yunus behind the kit. This is a person who obviously has a passion for drumming and music.\n\nTrying to pick a favorite track off this album is going to be next to impossible. Could it be the title track, \"DMNS\", with the nonstop breakdown and a chorus made for arenas accompanied by a terror inducing demonic laugh? Maybe \"Trying to Survive\" with one of the best lyrics that tugs at your heart strings. You know for a fact that hearing \"Anxiety, my constant friend. Always will be there 'til the very end\" will leave you with chills going down your spine when you hear it live. Perhaps it will be \"Broken\" as it leaves you wanting to m"
  },
