1963's \"Lilies of the Field,\" Sidney Poitier broke racial barriers, becoming the first Black actor to take home this top honor at the Oscars.\n\nMore common are the plethora of Best Actor Oscars representing personal milestones. At the 1981 Academy Awards, for example, legend Robert De Niro took home his"
