ckly established herself as a premier Spanish language teacher–capable of reaching and teaching students who find language acquisition particularly challenging while also inspiring our elite linguists who pursue the breadth of our AP curriculum. She is an engaging instructor who is constantly varying the pace and activity of lessons while reinforcing the objective for the day. She has been a respected champion for diversity, equity, and inclusion initiatives in the Upper School over the"
