    "snippet": "---\ntitle: PETER LIM PARTNERS WELLINGTON COLLEGE INTERNATIONAL TO SET UP SCHOOLS IN 3 SOUTHEAST ASIAN COUNTRIES\ndate: 2022-02-23\n---\nAmit AgarwalCO-FOUNDER,\n\nUNISON GROUP\n\nAmit Agarwal hails from a prominent family of educationists and philanthropists in Dehra Dun. An illustrious management graduate and eminent scholar with an eye for perfection, Amit Agarwal is a visionary who believes in 'Walk the Talk' philosophy and leads by example. His hard work resulted in the establishment of new Group institutions in Dehra Dun and Delhi NCR, in a short span of time, bringing accolades to the Group.\n\nA young and dynamic leader, he is an epitome of patience, practicality, perseverance and precision and extremely far sighted in his vision, and commands high respect in the academic fraternity. He envisions to create and nurture self-motivated professionals who will make a significant contribution towards the global society as a whole.\n\nAnuj Aggarwal CO-FOUNDER,\n\nUNISON GROUP\n\nAnuj Aggarwal, an alumnus of Saïd Business School, University of Oxford, is closely associated with spearheading the Group's initiatives. Deeply associated with the cause of education, Anuj Aggarwal is an incisive 'edupreneur' and humanitarian, widely credited with being one of the pioneers in changing the educational landscape of the region, dating back to over two decades.\n\nA second-generation entrepreneur, he is driven by the core philosophy of infusing 'Growth with Goodness' through his vision of nation-building. Nation-building, for him, means transforming the educational landscape of India by playing an instrumental role in creating institutions of transformational education that will continue to influence and nurture the country's youth for decades to come. He has always maintained that access to quality education is the most potent tool of transformation and that building successful institutions is dependent on forging enduring partnerships and creating new knowledge.\n\nScott BryanINTERNATIONAL DIRECTOR,\n\nWCI\n\nScott has a thorough understanding of the UK independent sector coupled with a wide range of international experience from more than 20 years working in education. His school leadership experience includes three successful Headships; in the UK, UAE and more recently as a founding Head in Switzerland. He was also Strategic Director at a leading UK Independent School, including responsibility for developing international business. Scott is responsible for developing WCI's schools"
  },
