    "snippet": "---\ntitle: Religion Book Deals: December 13, 2023\nauthor: Ann Byle\ndate: 2023-12-12\n---\nTyndale Lands Francine Rivers' Latest\n\nTyndale House fiction publisher Karen Watson bought world English/world Spanish and audio rights from Danielle Egan-Miller of Browne & Miller Literary Associates to bestselling author Francine Rivers' next novel, tentatively titled Mercy. A 2026 publication is planned. Readers of Rivers' 1991 megahit Redeeming Love and her recent bestseller The Lady's Mine will recognize the 1870s California setting. Mercy \"explores the cost of revenge\" while following a woman who must choose between cutting ties with her father or the man she's fallen in love with.\n\nClaude Atcho Moves to WaterBrook\n\nJevon Bolden of Embolden Media Group sold world rights to WaterBrook editor Jamey Lapeyrolerie for Word and Time by pastor and teacher Claude Atcho (Reading Black Books, Brazos), an ordained priest in the Anglican Church of North America and a teacher. The book, which is slated to release in fall 2025, is \"a fusion of scriptural and devotional reflections\" timed with the church liturgical calendar, according to the publisher.\n\nApples and Honey Nabs A Robot for Shabbat\n\nDena Neusner, executive editor at Apples & Honey Press, an imprint of Behrman House, has acquired world rights from Erzsi Deak of Hen & Ink Literary Agency to Robot Shabbat by Laura Gehl, children's book author and doctor of neuroscience from Georgetown University. The picture book for ages 2-5 follows a young girl who builds a robot to help her prepare for Shabbat. The book is slated for publication in fall 2024 and will be illustrated by artist David Williams, who was represented by Sarah Thomas of the Bright Group US Inc.\n\nParaclete Takes an Advent Celebration for Families\n\nLillian Miao, director at Paraclete Press, acquired world rights from Karen Neumair at Credo Communications to The Joy of Advent: Family Celebrations for Advent and the Twelve Days of Christmas, written by Rebecca Grabill and Stephen Grabill, and illustrated by Clare Therese Gray, who is unagented. This 37-day guided celebration of the season for families is slated for publication October 1"
