    "snippet": "---\ntitle: 'The Da Vinci Code' author's next book to be released: How to buy\nauthor: Molly Walsh; Mwalsh Com\ndate: 2024-01-08\n---\nNEW YORK -- Thriller novelist Dan Brown, best known for the blockbuster \"The Da Vinci Code,\" announced his next book will be published this year.\n\nPublisher Doubleday Books announced Wednesday that \"The Secret of Secrets\" will follow protagonist Robert Langdon, esteemed professor of symbology as he travels to Prague to New York to London, evading an assassin and ponders the depths of human consciousness. The book, which is available for pre-order now, will be published Sept. 9.\n\nThe book is also available to pre-order online on Amazon, Bookshop.org and at Barnes & Noble.\n\n\"Langdon finds himself targeted by a powerful organization and hunted by a chilling assailant sprung from Prague's most ancient mythology. As the plot expands into London and New York, Langdon desperately searches . . . for answers. In a thrilling race through the dual worlds of futuristic science and mystical lore, he uncovers a shocking truth about a secret project that will forever change the way we think about the human mind,\" Doubleday's synopsis of the book reads.\n\nBrown has set previous books in France, Italy and Spain among other countries and researches his locations in person. He said in a statement that his fascination with Prague \"began with its deep history of mysticism and the occult. It is a labyrinth of enigmatic sites — an ideal backdrop for a Robert Langdon thriller –- a city of secrets, both ancient and modern,\" according to the Associated Press.\n\nDoubleday plans to release the book in at least a dozen countries, including Czech Republic, Turkey, Spain and Finland. Brown's other novels include \"Angels & Demons,\" \"The Lost Symbol\" and \"Inferno.\"\n\n\"Writing it has been an unforgettable journey of discovery,\" Brown said in a statement.\n\nStories by Molly Walsh\n\n- R&B icon dies; family reveals film about his life is in the works\n\n- Big win for A-list couple as judge tosses $400 million lawsuit\n\n- More than 19,000 cases of popular soda pop recalled over labeling issue\n\n- Reporter shot by rubber bullet while on-air during Los Angeles protests\n\n- United Airlines reveals new collab to improve in-flight entertainment"
