    "snippet": "---\ntitle: Soundtracks of Television: 'Tell Me Lies'\nauthor: Q V Hough\ndate: 2022-09-08\n---\nThe Tell Me Lies soundtrack includes music by Tune-Yards, MGMT and Amy Winehouse. This info article contains spoilers and song details for Meaghan Oppenheimer's Hulu series. Visit the Soundtracks of Television section for more Vague Visages music guides.\n\nTell Me Lies stars Grace Van Patten as Lucy Albright, a college student who obsesses over a male classmate. Jackson White co-stars as Stephen DeMarco, the protagonist's love interest who spends time with his ex-girlfriend. The storyline follows Lucy as her life spirals out of control after the sudden death of a roommate. Composer Jay Wadley (Fire Island) scored the Hulu series; music supervisor Liza Richardson (Barry) selected the featured needle-drops. Here's every song in Tell Me Lies, an adaptation of Carola Lovering's 2018 book.\n\nRead More at VV — Soundtracks of Television: 'Reservation Dogs'\n\nTell Me Lies Soundtrack: Every Song in Season 1, Episode 1 \"Lightning Strikes\"\n\n- \"Doin' It Right\" by FEIN (00:02): The Tell Me Lies soundtrack song begins during a car sequence. Music plays through the stereo. Lucy switches the radio station.\n\n- \"Crazy\" by Gnarls Barkley (00:05): Lucy prepares for a party. The track continues during a transition scene. Lucy drinks a glass of champagne.\n\n- \"Time to Pretend\" by MGMT (00:11): The music kicks in during a car scene. Lucy travels with her mother. She arrives at the Baird College campus.\n\n- \"Bounce If You Want To\" by Da Wolf Pac (00:17): The Tell Me Lies soundtrack song accompanies a party sequence. Lucy walks around with Bree (Catherine Missal) and Pippa (Sonia Mena). Wrigley chats with his former roommate, Evan (Branden Cook).\n\n- \"Drops of Jupiter\" by Train (00:32): A memorial sequence begins. A students sings the 2001 hit. Lucy talks about the lyrics.\n\n- \"That's Right\" by Marcus Latief Scott (00:33): Lucy hangs out at a party. She walks away from Pippa and Wrigley.\n\n-"
