    "snippet": "---\ntitle: 6 Anime Releases I'm Excited for in 2021\ndate: 2020-12-06\n---\n6 Anime Releases I'm Excited for in 2021\n\nIf there's anything we can collectively celebrate right now, it's that this cursed year is just about through. But even though we're all looking forward to 2020 being over, I can't deny that it was a pretty decent year as far as new anime was concerned. From movies like Demon Slayer: Mugen Train to romantic comedies like TONIKAWA: Over the Moon for You, anime fans everywhere were treated to some awesome new releases throughout a troubling year.\n\nBut as great as those titles are, we have plenty more new anime ahead of us in 2021. So without further ado, these are (in no particular order) the new seasons, reboots, and fresh original releases I'm looking forward to in the coming year!\n\n1. My Hero Academia Season 5 (March)\n\nThe superhero saga continues! Following the (spoiler alert) defeat of Hood at the hands of redeemed hero Endeavor, the students of UA High School prepare for their greatest test yet: a training competition in which they must do battle against their fellow young heroes. Bonds will be tested and strength will be shown off in what may very well be the most thrilling season of My Hero Academia so far!\n\n2. SK8 the Infinity (January)\n\nTony Hawk fans, rejoice! From the director that brought us Free! and Banana Fish, SK8 the Infinity is a skateboarding anime series that looks sure to be a blast in every way you can think of. Our hero, Reki, gets involved in a secret skateboarding tournament known only as \"S\" in which the goal is to survive until the end of the track. With plenty of colorful and aggressive opponents to face, Reki will have a long way to go before he can claim the prize. I'd wager that this will be a visual treat from start to finish, so I'll be watching for sure.\n\n3. Horimiya (January)\n\nIf you were to use an old proverb to describe the premise of this anime series, \"Don't judge a book by its cover\" would be the one. Kyōko Hori is praised for being a hardworking and intelligent student, but she has been robbed of a social life due to her parents being away at work all the time, while"
