ion, BMI allows comparison between children of the same sex and age. For children, a BMI that is less than the fifth percentile is underweight and above the 95th percentile is considered obese.[3]\n\n- Severely underweight - BMI less than 16.5kg/m^2\n\n- Underweight - BMI under 18.5 kg/m^2\n\n- Normal weight - BMI greater than or equal to 18."
