    "snippet": "---\ntitle: I got divorced twice before 30 — but I still believe in happily ever after\ndate: 2024-03-20\n---\nI got divorced twice before 30 — but I still believe in happily ever after\n\nThree-ring circus?\n\nA Florida life coach who got divorced twice before 30 says she's dating again — and wouldn't rule out tying the knot for a third time.\n\n\"I still have a little guard up because I am scared of pain, but because I have navigated divorce and breakups before, I know I have the tools to cope,\" Marissa Baker, 32, told SWNS.\n\nThe millennial Elizabeth Taylor met her first husband in college while studying sports management — they had a whirlwind relationship that quickly went from \"passionate\" to \"intense.\"\n\nBaker would tell herself that every relationship has ups and downs, so the pair married in December 2014.\n\n\"When it was good, it was really good, but when it was bad, it was really bad,\" Baker said of her first marriage, which ended in divorce in June 2016.\n\nBefore the divorce was finalized, the Naples resident found herself in a relationship with a man who would become her second husband. They met on Tinder.\n\n\"It was really easy for me to say that the first husband was the problem, so I am not going to take ownership of my issues — I am not going to heal, and I am going to jump into this other relationship,\" Baker shared.\n\nShe added: \"I was not a great partner — and what I mean by that is my ex was always asking for not very hard things like doing the dishes or the laundry and I just couldn't get myself to do those.\"\n\nShe married hubby No. 2 in 2019 and got divorced in November 2021.\n\n\"I had just turned 29. I had a lot of fear and a lot of shame about leaving it all because I thought, 'Damn, how did I get myself here again?'\" Baker recalled.\n\n\"As useless as I think shame is, I do think having that fear and shame really forced me to reflect and say, 'How did I contribute to the problem?'\" she continued. \"I worked on areas I needed to fix and really concentrated on how I got myself into this situation in the first place.\"\n\nAfter her second divorce, Baker decided to focus on herself, and she met her \"platonic soulmate\" — Patty"
