    "snippet": "---\ntitle: Blog Writing: 10 Years Later\nauthor: Full\ndate: 2021-06-06\n---\nThis week marks 10 years since I wrote my first blog post. And that post itself was really only a quote. It was called Calling All Magic-Bean Buyers. And then, simply this:\n\n\"If you are a dreamer, come in. If you are a dreamer, a wisher, a liar, a hoper, a prayer, a magic-bean-buyer. If you're a pretender, come sit by my fire, for we have some flax-golden tales to spin. Come in! Come in!\" ~Shel Silverstein\n\nToday I simply want to say thank you for coming in. Thank you for being the kindest community on the Internet.\n\nTo those of you who comment and send emails and to those of you who read silently and would never comment in a million years – thank you.\n\nTo those of you who I've met in real life because of this space and to those of you who I will never have the privilege of meeting on earth – thank you.\n\nTo my fellow writers, readers, Parks & Rec lovers, bench-dwellers, Tuesday friends and fellow magic-bean buyers – thank you.\n\nWithout each of you, I'm simply talking to myself. So I am ever grateful to you for reading. Here's to the next 10 years of writing on a blog, however many changes and new forms that might take!\n\nOkay. I'm done with my speech. Now in honor of 2016, here are my Top 16 Most Read Posts of all Time:\n\n- One Thing Your Daughter Doesn't Need You to Say\n\n- 12 Things Your Daughter Needs You to Say\n\n- Dare to Paint Your Kitchen Cabinets Black\n\n- Choosing the One You Least Expect\n\n- A Staying Prayer for Mothers of College Freshmen\n\n- One Thing That Will Make Your Soul Explode\n\n- 14 Ways to Make Mediocre Art\n\n- The Spiritual Discipline of Wearing Better Pants\n\n- A Sending Prayer for College Freshmen\n\n- For the Girls\n\n- Hush\n\n- For Those of You Who Don't Comment on Blogs\n\n- Becoming a Soul Minimalist\n\n- A Sweet Cup of No Expectations\n\n- What's It Like to be An Introverted Woman in Church Circles\n\n- One Alternative to Pessimism and Optimism\n\nAlso, I'm embarrassed to say my"
