    "snippet": "---\ndate: 2024-06-27\n---\n- The 'Empire State of Mind' singer has a blended family with her husband, producer and rapper Swizz Beatz – his 3 children from previous relationships joined their recent trip to Italy\n\n- Keys' eldest stepson Prince Nasir starred in Charge It to the Game alongside Snoop Dogg and Dr Dre's sons, while her youngest son Genesis wants to become friends with Taylor Swift and Billie Eilish\n\nAlicia Keys' new Broadway musical Hell's Kitchen, inspired by her life and featuring her music, won big at the Tony Awards last week, snagging best actress for Maleah Joi Moon and featured actress for Kecia Lewis.\n\nKeys brought along her sons Egypt, 13, and Genesis, nine, plus her stepson Kasseem Jr. Her parents, Terria Joseph and Craig Cook, were there too, making it a full family affair.\n\nAdvertisement\n\nDespite being one of the greatest piano players and songwriters of her time, Keys, 43, also shines as a loving mum. She and her husband, producer and rapper Swizz Beatz, 45, whose real name is Kasseem Dean, have seamlessly blended their families.\n\nKeys shares Egypt and Genesis with him. Together, they have a blended family with his children: Prince Nasir, 23, Kasseem Jr, 17, and Nicole, 16, making it a lively household of five kids.\n\nSo what do we know about Keys' five children – and stepchildren?\n\nPrince Nasir Dean, Keys' eldest stepchild, was born to Swizz Beatz and his ex Nicole Levy in October 2000, per Hollywood Life. Following his father's footsteps, Prince Nasir makes music as Note Marcato and gained viral fame in 2020 for his skeleton face paint at the Grammy Awards, making it his signature look."
