    "snippet": "---\ntitle: Keith LaGore\ndate: 2013-12-31\n---\nR. Keith LaGore, 71, of Fishers, passed away on Tuesday, December 31, 2013, at St. Vincent Heart Center of Indiana in Indianapolis. He was born on August 15, 1942, to Joseph and Rosetta (Kindel) LaGore in Detroit, Michigan.\n\nKeith worked in finance at General Motors for 33 years before retiring. He continued working as a financial consultant for GM after his retirement. He earned his Master's degree at Wayne State University, and his undergraduate at Western Michigan University. He was a very active member in his church, First United Methodist Church in Noblesville.\n\nHe is survived by wife, Margo LaGore; children, Rick (Terry) LaGore and Jennifer LaGore; grandchildren, Alex & Grant LaGore and Elizabeth & Amanda Hall; and step-grandchildren, Jeff, Katy & Michael Perrin.\n\nIn addition to his parents, he was preceded in death by brother, Jerry LaGore.\n\nServices will be held at 2:00 pm on Saturday, January 4, 2014, at First United Methodist Church, 2051 Monument Street in Noblesville, with Pastor Dick Judson officiating. Visitation will be Friday, January 3, 2014 from 4:00 pm to 8:00 pm at Randall & Roberts Fishers Mortuary, 12010 Allisonville Road in Fishers. Burial will be at Crownland Cemetery in Noblesville.\n\nMemorial contributions may be made to Western Michigan University Foundation, please write, \"LaGore Scholarship\" in the memo line on checks, C/O Randall & Roberts Funeral Home, 1685 Westfield Road, Noblesville, IN 46062.\n\nKeith worked in finance at General Motors for 33 years before retiring. He continued working as a financial consultant for GM after his retirement. He earned his Master's degree at Wayne State University, and his undergraduate at Western Michigan University. He was a very active member in his church, First United Methodist Church in Noblesville.\n\nHe is survived by wife, Margo LaGore; children, Rick (Terry) LaGore and Jennifer LaGore; grandchildren, Alex & Grant LaG