    "snippet": "---\ntitle: Author Frequently Asked Questions\nauthor: Q Does the license\ndate: 2018-01-01\n---\nAuthor Frequently Asked Questions\n\nTable of Contents\n\nwhy open access?\n\n- Why are we doing this?\n\n- What do the Harvard open-access policies provide?\n\n- Why do the open-access policies include an automatic or default license? Why not just suggest authors individually retain a license for open-access distribution?\n\n- What are the advantages for authors?\n\n- What will Harvard do with the articles covered by its license?\n\npolicy and license basics\n\n- What kinds of writings do the open-access policies cover?\n\n- What version of a scholarly article should authors deposit in the repository?\n\n- Does the license to Harvard apply to articles I wrote before the policy was adopted?\n\n- Does the policy apply to articles I write after leaving Harvard?\n\n- How do I request a waiver of the Harvard license?\n\n- Does the license to Harvard apply to co-authored papers?\n\n- What if my article is subject to the NIH Public Access Policy?\n\n- Are students covered by the Harvard open-access policies?\n\n- What if I'm a non-faculty author and would like my scholarly articles to be covered by an open-access license?\n\n- I'm a graduate student. How do I make my thesis or dissertation open access?\n\n- What is the individual open-access license?\n\ncommon concerns\n\n- Can my articles be used as the basis of derivative works by other authors?\n\n- Is the university acquiring ownership of my writing?\n\n- Will Harvard ever sell articles for profit or allow others to do so?\n\n- What if a journal publisher refuses to publish my article because of this prior license to Harvard?\n\n- Does this website provide legal advice to me?\n\ndepositing articles in dash\n\n- Should I include my article in DASH even if I have gotten a waiver for it?\n\n- Should I include my article in DASH even if the work is not covered by the Harvard license?\n\n- What is a dark deposit?\n\n- I've already published a large number of articles. What's the easiest way to get all of them into DASH?\n\nusing an author addendum\n\n- What is an author addendum?\n\n- How do I use an author addendum?\n\n- What if my article has co-authors?\n\n- What if the journal publisher refuses to accept my addendum or wants to negotiate it?\n\n- What if a publisher tells me I don't need the addendum because the publisher's agreement already permits immediate posting of the article in an institutional open-access repository?\n\nWHY OPEN ACCESS"
