    "snippet": "---\ntitle: Completed Theses\ndate: 2015-10-24\n---\nCompleted Theses\n\nCompleted M.A. Theses\n\nTo complete their M.A. degree, History students are required to write and defend a final research paper (40-60 pages) under the direction of a faculty mentor. Students concentrating in medieval history develop a proposal and research paper through the proseminar/seminar sequence. Students concentrating in modern history develop (normally within their coursework) a research proposal in the fall semester; in the spring, they complete the project by taking a research tutorial with a faculty member in which they produce a research proposal and paper.\n\n2024\n\nThe French Revolution and the Politics of Beauty: Theresa Tallien and Charlotte Corday\n\nRuby Archbold\n\nMentor: Dr. Thierry Rigogne\n\nComfort Women as Military Supplies: The Origins, Structure, and Management of Comfort Women System in the Japanese Military (1931-1945)\n\nAnna Bartsch\n\nMentor: Dr. Grace Shen\n\nPermanent Petition: Towards a Mesohistory of the Archives of the United Trusteeship and Non-Self-Governing Territory Arrangements\n\nAnthony Coxeter\n\nMentor: Dr. Christopher Dietrich\n\nByzantine Latinity and Planoudes' Ovidiana Graeca\n\nQianyi Fu\n\nMentor: Dr. Scott Bruce\n\nHagiographical Portrayal and Political Participation in the Passiones of Late Merovingian Burgundy\n\nRyan Sheehan\n\nMentor: Dr. Scott Bruce\n\nRacial Segregation and Housing Discrimination on Long Island (c. 1920- c.1970)\n\nBlake Walton\n\nMentor: Dr. Daniel Soyer\n\n2023\n\nThe New York, Westchester & Boston Railway 1912-1937: The construction and collapse of a Unique Railroad in Historical Context\n\nReece Brosco\n\nMentor: Dr. Mattie Armstrong-Price\n\nThe Creation of the Enemy: The Dawn of the Inter-American Cold War Anti-Ideologies in the 1940s\n\nFrancisco Javier Calderon Abullarade\n\nMentor: Dr. Christopher Dietrich\n\nThe Irish-Scots: Across and In Between the Kingdoms of Ireland and Scotland During t